Before a GitHub job likely to make more than about 100 REST calls, run `gh api rate_limit`. Stop before starting or continuing if fewer than 1,000 core requests remain. Send at most `min(4, remaining - 999)` REST calls per batch. Wait for all responses, then use the lowest core `X-RateLimit-Remaining` header (`gh api --include`) or rerun the quota check at no primary quota cost before sending more. Leave at least a minute between status checks in a loop.

Prefer one GraphQL query per repository over REST calls for individual pull requests. Prefer local Git (`git fetch`, `git log`, and `git merge-base`) over REST for questions about commits, ancestry, or merge methods. Prefer conditional requests when rereading a resource. Send its `ETag` with `If-None-Match`, or use `If-Modified-Since`. An authenticated 304 response costs no primary quota.
